  "notes": [
    "Voice has two explicit transmission modes: Open Microphone and Push to Talk. Push to Talk sends only while its bound key is held, including quiet speech; releasing it closes the send gate. Stale microphone frames are discarded at input boundaries.",
    "Green audio symbols beside player names replace the SPEAKING text in the lobby and game. They follow actual transmitted speech; the separate microphone meter still measures your input when PTT is released.",
    "Lobby voice reaches the whole crew; maze voice stays directional with smooth proximity fade. Routine lobby updates no longer close voice settings or abort microphone setup. Input, held-key, mute, privacy and four-peer Relay mixing checks accompany this release.",
    "Repeater footsteps are dry concrete heel/sole recordings without the rejected metallic taps or wet squeaks. Original mouth clicks and chase scream are retained. No new downloads.",
    "Reaver retains the owner-supplied massive footstep recording at its original pitch, with stronger 24m distance scale, 90m range and a deeper hall return. The Repeater uses a separate footstep profile.",
    "Close the game completely, then choose Check for updates and Update & restart. All players should update; saved settings and progression rules are retained."
  ],
